      "writtenOn": "2022-03-25T13:40:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The fact that you had to change this suggests that if the socket is not bound, getAddressFromFileDescriptor doesn\u0027t return null but returns an empty address. Is this a bug in the current code that you are fixing? If so, that suggests that currently, unbound sockets will get EX_TYPE_FILTER_SOCKET_LOCAL_ADDRESS_CHANGED, but after we push this change to the field in a mainline update, unbound sockets will start getting a SocketNotBoundExxception. Could this break existing clients somehow?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 94,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 94,
        "endChar": 87
      },
      "revId": "55c70679818647f5ce04b6b17e403e4d374cd7ea",
